{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For your servant became surety for the lad.</b> He means that he will go down with sorrow to Sheol upon him, for even after all this that we said to him, the old man was unwilling to send him until I became a guarantor for him and he trusted in me, and therefore let your servant, I pray, remain instead of him. And if the meaning of \"and bring down your servants\" (Genesis 44:33) is according to its plain sense, he says: we are the ones who cause the death of the old man in evil, for I became surety for him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:48.430535481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}